docs {
  # v5 Intervention > Recovery and Resubmission Scenarios

  Checks that the provider recovers from synchronization failures or missing
  records. Steps 1–8 **delete** a subset of the records you published (with your
  own credentials). You then run your **normal synchronization** (not
  hand-crafted API calls), and steps 9–14 confirm the restored data matches what
  was there before.

  > **Run this scenario last.** After it runs, ids captured by the earlier
  > scenarios point at deleted records, so earlier steps can't be re-run without
  > starting again from "Publish and Maintain Intervention Definitions".
  > Steps 1–8 can be re-run safely: a record that is already gone counts as deleted.

  > **Run it in one Bruno session.** Values captured by the earlier scenarios live
  > only in the open Bruno session. If Bruno is closed or the environment is
  > switched before step 14, steps 9–14 fail with "Missing required variable" and
  > can't recover, because the records they would read were deleted by design.
  > Start again from "Publish and Maintain Intervention Definitions" (Sample Data
  > users: run `Sample Data › MTSS › Reset` first).
  >
  > Steps marked `[OPTION 1]` or `[OPTION 2]` belong to that staff option only;
  > skip the ones for the option you did not certify.

  ## Prerequisites

  * All earlier scenarios completed on your chosen staff option.
  * The `first` Intervention holds only the certification records (the `first`
    StudentInterventionAssociation and its attendance events). Any other record
    that references it makes step 7 fail with 409 Conflict.
  * Your product still holds the source data for every record below.

  ## Scenarios tasks

  1. __DELETE__ Remove the `third` attendance event (sample: 2026-09-10 Partial).
  2. __DELETE__ Remove the `first` StudentInterventionAssociation.
  3. __DELETE__ Remove the `first` attendance event.
  4. __DELETE__ Remove the `second` attendance event.
  5. __DELETE__ Remove the `fifth` attendance event.
  6. __DELETE__ [optional] Remove the `sixth` attendance event (only if you recorded it).
  7. __DELETE__ Remove the `first` Intervention (nothing references it any more).
  8. __DELETE__ [OPTION 2] Remove the `first` StaffCohortAssociation. The Cohort is left in place.
  9. __CREATE__ **After your normal synchronization:** the `first` Intervention is restored with its latest _endDate_ and _maxDosage_.
  10. __DELETE__ The `second` Intervention (deleted earlier by you) did not reappear.
  11. __CREATE__ The `first` StudentInterventionAssociation is restored with its latest _dosage_; the `second` one did not reappear.
  12. __CREATE__ ALL attendance events are restored: checks pass, the `second` event keeps its updated duration, the deleted `fourth` event did not reappear, and assigned vs. delivered results equal those of "AssignedVersusDeliveredDosage".
  13. __CREATE__ [OPTION 1] The `first` Intervention lists the same staff as after the OPTION 1 update.
  14. __CREATE__ [OPTION 2] The `first` StaffCohortAssociation is restored (latest _endDate_), it is the Cohort's only one, and the `first` StudentInterventionAssociation still references the Cohort.

  ## Expected state after synchronization

  | Resource                           | Record (natural key, sample)                     | Expected                                                  |
  | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
  | StudentInterventionAttendanceEvent | 604863 / READ-T2-001 / 2026-09-10 / Partial      | Restored: interventionDuration 15                         |
  | StudentInterventionAssociation     | 604863 / 255901 / READ-T2-001                    | Restored: dosage 900; OPTION 2: cohortReference GRP-A     |
  | StudentInterventionAttendanceEvent | 604863 / READ-T2-001 / 2026-09-08 / In Attendance | Restored: interventionDuration 30                        |
  | StudentInterventionAttendanceEvent | 604863 / READ-T2-001 / 2026-09-09 / In Attendance | Restored: interventionDuration **25** (latest, not 30)   |
  | StudentInterventionAttendanceEvent | 604863 / READ-T2-001 / 2026-09-11 / Excused Absence | Restored: interventionDuration 0                       |
  | StudentInterventionAttendanceEvent | 604863 / READ-T2-001 / 2026-09-14 / Session Not Held | Restored, if recorded                                 |
  | Intervention                       | 255901 / READ-T2-001                             | Restored with the latest values; OPTION 1: staffs 207288 only |
  | StaffCohortAssociation (OPTION 2)  | 207288 / READ-T2-001-GRP-A / 255901 / 2026-08-24 | Restored: endDate 2026-12-18                              |

  Records that must **not** reappear: Intervention ATTD-T2-001, the 604854
  StudentInterventionAssociation, the 2026-09-11 Unexcused Absence event, the
  207289 StaffCohortAssociation (OPTION 2), and staff 207289 on the
  Intervention (OPTION 1).

  Restored records get a new resource `id` from the ODS/API; certification
  compares natural keys and values, not ids.
}
